# Follow-up probe, same cell family. -3.play found that pressing `key
# Escape` from a daily fight (any daily fight, class:6=priest:shadow was
# used there) lands on the ordinary RAID roster/class-select screen, and
# that screen's "first room" banner named the *daily's* boss (The
# Bloodgorged) rather than the citadel's real first fight -- src/main.ts's
# updateRaidSetup() only sets `encounter = firstFight()` when NEXT is
# pressed on the actual raid size/difficulty screen, which this path never
# goes through. This checks what pressing the roster's own PULL/"WALK IN"
# button actually does from that state: a real raid walk-in with a stale
# label, or an attempt to fight the daily's boss as if it were the
# citadel's front door. Escaping early (not waiting for the fight to
# resolve) to save the ~130s a full wipe costs -- the earlier run showed
# `encounter` is whatever the daily set regardless of outcome, so nothing
# about *when* Escape is pressed should matter to this question.
open
tap daily
tap class:6
tap start
waitscreen fight 15
wait 3
key Escape
targets
shot roster-after-escape
state
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot after-pull
targets
